    "body": "Contextual revisions could choose an earlier word as the owner or suppress a valid dependent revision. This adds a learned nonpositive correction to the shared native writer, conditioned on inherited lexical-prime fields, the exterior separator and directed endpoint separation. For example, the retained model now answers the owner-first query after “selvi in Dusk Ridge. selvi now in Copper Vale.” with “selvi is in Copper Vale.” and commits the correct owner/version link.\n\nThe retained artifact is `blake3:6f5ab4f3e5cad068d72f72795fead8fb1b371c009e5935448c8c20df0794d778`. Its complete field-composition parent is frozen and reconstructs byte-for-byte. Serving uses bounded integer/table scoring with the inherited geometric operators; no phrase parser, response payload, matrix product or provider is added. Layout 1 remains byte-exactly readable. The earlier candidate that suppressed 12 valid dependency revisions is preserved as rejected evidence.\n\nExecuted locally:\n\n- New construction: 60/60 outputs and target records; 76/76 older dependency/name targets and 997/997 inherited comparisons. These overlapping populations are described in the evidence.\n- New post-selection identity draw: 28/28 labelled responses/records and eight unchanged inherited comparisons. Both extension-removal and gap-removal controls restore parent behavior.\n- Structural stress: 16/16 correct target records, 15/16 responses. Full older preservation, including 663 construction answers, 48 dependent and 28 name cases, passes. Fourteen prior semantic/control reports remain exactly unchanged.\n- Native API: 215 passing checks. 49 unique focused tests, including nine actual-artifact allocation/checkpoint checks and the integer-kernel source guard, pass. Generated retained Rust snippets compile and execute. Cargo formatting and capability wording checks pass.\n\nThe reversed-first-fact read error remains: recent routing can select a historical phrase despite correct current records, while the same records answer correctly after recent-window eviction. General prose/reasoning/Rust synthesis, alpha/frontier capability and complete-path energy savings remain unqualified. New-artifact browser/WASM/HTTP and the blanket full suite are not run.\n\nThis cycle's immutable evidence records 3216.860 model seconds, all rejected/failed-run charges, the authorized extension and conservative storage accounting. No unique material was deleted and no paid external compute was used. The five GitHub queue statuses are compatibility acknowledgements; they do not execute these local checks.\n\nSee [the result](docs/native_geometric_owner_revision_973.md) and [machine-readable evidence](docs/evidence/native_geometric_owner_revision_973.json). The current-state pointer and next source/version selection step are updated.\n\nReferences #973\n",
